      ],
      "clean_question": "Classify each statement as true or false.\n\na. A population is the complete set of units about which a study seeks information.\n\nb. Examining only some population units constitutes a census.\n\nc. A quantitative variable is also called a categorical variable.\n\nd. Statistical inference uses sample measurements to generalize about a population.\n\ne. Describing the important features of a set of measurements is called statistical inference.",
      "clean_answer": "a. **True.**\n\nb. **False.** A census examines every unit in the population.\n\nc. **False.** A categorical variable is qualitative, not quantitative.\n\nd. **True.**\n\ne. **False.** That task is descriptive statistics.",
      "expected_question_hash": "3d4a99d13f7874a1324762fb712587d657bc3ef54b6bb303cfdd8201a9f83192",
      "expected_answer_hash": "acebfdd1fa369d46cb35ac0b84aeb51159c27142e5f68cfabf6125ba78aaf21b",
