      "question_type": "简答题",
      "difficulty": 1,
      "keywords": [
        "quantitative variable",
        "qualitative variable"
      ],
      "clean_question": "Below we list several variables. Which of these variables are quantitative and which are qualitative? Explain.\n\na. The dollar amount on an accounts receivable invoice.\n\nb. The net profit for a company in 2005.\n\nc. The stock exchange on which a company's stock is traded.\n\nd. The national debt of the United States in 2005.\n\ne. The advertising medium (radio, television, or print) used to promote a product.",
      "clean_answer": "a. **Quantitative**, because an invoice amount is a numerical measurement.\n\nb. **Quantitative**, because net profit is a numerical amount.\n\nc. **Qualitative**, because the stock exchange is a category.\n\nd. **Quantitative**, because national debt is a numerical amount.\n\ne. **Qualitative**, because advertising medium identifies a category.",
      "expected_question_hash": "e54c31fefcff79c0c81cf13eb8f304cc71ccdbb1454a201a9cbae671a4e0ed81",
      "expected_answer_hash": "688dc9e596b4a3bb120c11355434e1ef3e290f5cd1ce832baf0f56f92d8297ff",
