      "decision": "rewrite",
      "question_type": "简答题",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "keywords": [
        "nominal variable",
        "ordinal variable"
      ],
      "clean_question": "Classify each qualitative variable as nominal or ordinal, and explain briefly.\n\na. Statistics course letter grade: A, B, C, D, or F\n\nb. Door choice on a game show: Door 1 or Door 2\n\nc. Personal computer ownership: yes or no\n\nd. Restaurant rating: one to five stars\n\ne. Income-tax filing status: married filing jointly, married filing separately, single, head of household, or qualifying widow(er)",
      "clean_answer": "a. **Ordinal**, because letter grades have a meaningful order.\n\nb. **Nominal**, because door numbers are labels with no ranking.\n\nc. **Nominal**, because yes and no are unordered categories.\n\nd. **Ordinal**, because higher star ratings indicate a higher rank.\n\ne. **Nominal**, because filing-status categories have no natural order.",
